-- title:
--   Universal property of the affine dilatation A[I/a]
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $I \subseteq A$ an ideal and $a \in A$, and let $C$ be a commutative $A$-algebra. Write [`AffineDilatation.Ring I a`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20) for the underlying type of [`AffineDilatation.subalgebra I a`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L17), the $A$-subalgebra $\mathrm{adjoin}_A(\mathtt{gen } I\ a)$ of the localisation `Localization.Away a` generated by the set `gen I a`; its members are the elements `divElem I a g hg` attached to the elements $g \in I$, which by `algebraMap_mul_divElem` satisfy $a \cdot \mathtt{divElem } I\ a\ g\ hg = g$ in `Localization.Away a`, so that the subalgebra is the classical $A[I/a]$. Assume that multiplication by $a$ is injective on $C$ (`IsSMulRegular C a`) and that the image of $I$ under $A \to C$ is contained in the principal ideal generated by the image of $a$, i.e. $I\,C \subseteq a\,C$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions about the type of $A$-algebra homomorphisms $A[I/a] \to C$: it is nonempty, and it is a subsingleton. Thus there is exactly one $A$-algebra map $A[I/a] \to C$.
--
--   This is the affine form of the universal property of a dilatation (Bosch–Lütkebohmert–Raynaud, 3.2, Proposition 1): a flat test object whose special fibre meets the closed subscheme cut out by $I$ factors uniquely through the dilatation. It is used for the construction of maps out of the dilated ring, in particular by [`AffineDilatation.exists_algHom_isLocalization_map`](thm.html#AffineDilatation.exists_algHom_isLocalization_map), by [`AffineDilatation.nonempty_algEquiv_tensorProduct_of_flat_of_map_eq`](thm.html#AffineDilatation.nonempty_algEquiv_tensorProduct_of_flat_of_map_eq), and in the Néron model infrastructure comparing restrictions of schemes along chains of closed subschemes with affine dilatations.
-- source:
